# Recorded OSC 133 FIFO traffic from a Bash session in Oxterm, plus the
# malformed lines the reader has to tolerate.
#
# One event per line: A is a prompt start, C<text> a command start, D<n> the
# exit status. The integration script writes these lines to a private FIFO and
# Oxterm reads them; nothing here is ever shown on screen.
#
# Lines beginning with # are not events. The reader drops them like any other
# unknown letter, which is also what happens when a future integration sends an
# event this version does not know about.
#
# tests/osc133_conformance.rs replays this file byte by byte and in one go, so
# an edit here that changes behaviour must be reflected in the expected events
# in that test. See docs/compatibility.md.
A
Ctrue
D0
A
Cgit status
D0
A
Cgrep -R "città 🚀" src
D1
A
# The shell failed to capture $?: the status is missing, not zero.
Cfalse
D
A
# Command text that looks like other events.
Cprintf 'A\nD1\n'
D0
A
# Padding a shell may leave around the command line.
C   ls -l ~/oxterm
D0
A
